Cell[TextData[{
 "Eight instructions in six layers: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"R", ",", "4"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"R", ",", "5"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " share the first, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"M", ",", "4"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"CNOT", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " share the fourth. And 18 qubit-steps of waiting, against 28 if every \
instruction had its own step \[LongDash] which is the point of section \
15.5.1, where partial parallelism multiplies the storage rate and ",
 StyleBox["\"to have a threshold, it is essential to do parallel gates, at \
least when the storage error rate is non-zero\"", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Where an idle fault goes is the part that is easy to get wrong, and the \
wrong answer is tempting. \"The end of the layer\" is not a point in time, \
because ",
 StyleBox["the instruction list is not ordered by layer",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": layer 1 holds instructions 1 and 5 while layer 2 holds instruction 2, so \
in emission order instruction 5 comes ",
 StyleBox["after", "TI"],
 " instruction 2."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "What is well defined is per qubit. The frame propagator walks the flat \
list, so for a fault on qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["q", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 " the only thing that matters is which instructions touching ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["q", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " run after it. A qubit idle in layer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " has no instruction in that layer, so the fault belongs after the last \
instruction touching ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["q", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 " in an ",
 StyleBox["earlier", "TI"],
 " layer \[LongDash] and at index 0, before the circuit, when none has run \
yet:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"layerOf", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"circuitInstructionLayers", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"bfCirc", "[", "\"\<Instructions\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "5"}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"circuitIdleAnchor", "[", 
