}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First, faults that fire no detector ",
 StyleBox["and", "TI"],
 " flip no observable \[LongDash] the ones a reset wipes before they reach \
anything. Keeping them only inflates the subset search a decoder has to do."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second, faults the channel cannot actually produce, meaning probability \
literally zero: bit-flip noise never makes a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],
 " or a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 ". These matter more than they look, because the minimum-weight decoder does \
not read probabilities. A zero-probability row left in the table can claim a \
detector pattern that a real fault should have had, and quietly make the \
decoder worse than the noise deserves. A symbolic rate is never dropped, \
since nothing can be concluded about it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],

Cell["Memory.wl \[LongDash] the memory experiment", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Prepare a codeword, run ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 " rounds of noisy syndrome extraction, read the data out perfectly at the \
end, decode the whole detector history, and ask whether the logical qubit \
survived."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],

Cell["Two limits bound the two routes:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],

